**Finding:** No security-related HTTP headers are set. The app is missing protections against clickjacking, MIME-type sniffing, XSS via reflected content, and information leakage via the `X-Powered-By: Express` header.

**Fix:** Use the `helmet` middleware — one line covers a large class of header-based vulnerabilities:

```js
const helmet = require('helmet');

// Must be applied BEFORE routes
app.use(helmet());

// helmet sets all of these by default:
// - Content-Security-Policy
// - X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
// - X-Frame-Options: SAMEORIGIN
// - Strict-Transport-Security (HSTS)
// - X-DNS-Prefetch-Control
// - Referrer-Policy
// Removes X-Powered-By automatically
```

