### 9. No HTTPS Enforcement

**Problem:** The app binds to port 3000 over plain HTTP with no redirect or HSTS enforcement. Credentials and data are transmitted in plaintext.

**Fix:** If terminating TLS in-app (not recommended for most deployments — prefer a reverse proxy):
```js
const https = require('https');
const fs = require('fs');

const options = {
  key: fs.readFileSync(process.env.TLS_KEY_PATH),
  cert: fs.readFileSync(process.env.TLS_CERT_PATH),
};

https.createServer(options, app).listen(443);

// Redirect HTTP → HTTPS
const http = require('http');
http.createServer((req, res) => {
  res.writeHead(301, { Location: `https://${req.headers.host}${req.url}` });
  res.end();
