### 🟡 Finding 7 — No Centralized Error Handler (OWASP A05, A09)

**File:** `app.js` (entire file)

**Problem:** There is no error-handling middleware. Unhandled errors in Express will leak stack traces to clients, revealing file paths, dependency versions, and internal logic. This is **Security Misconfiguration (A05)** and **Security Logging & Monitoring Failures (A09)**.

**Recommendation:**
```js
// logger.js — use a real logger, never console.log in production
const pino = require('pino'); // npm install pino
const logger = pino({ level: process.env.LOG_LEVEL || 'info' });

// app.js — register LAST, after all routes
app.use((err, req, res, next) => {
  // Log internally with full detail
  logger.error({ err, url: req.url, method: req.method }, 'Unhandled error');

  // Respond externally with NO internal detail
  const statusCode = err.status || err.statusCode || 500;
  res.status(statusCode).json({
    error: statusCode < 500 ? err.message : 'An internal error occurred',
  });
});
```

