## Finding 8 — Unhandled Errors Leak Stack Traces (OWASP A05: Security Misconfiguration)

**Severity: Low–Medium**

There is no global error handler. Express's default error handler will expose stack traces in development mode, and any unhandled async rejection will crash the process in Node.js ≥ 15.

**Recommended fix:**
```js
// Catch-all error handler — must be defined LAST, after all routes
app.use((err, req, res, next) => {
  // Log full error internally (use a structured logger like pino/winston)
  console.error({ err, reqId: req.id, path: req.path });

  // Return a safe, generic message to the client
  const statusCode = err.statusCode ?? 500;
  res.status(statusCode).json({
    error: process.env.NODE_ENV === 'production'
      ? 'An unexpected error occurred'
      : err.message, // Only expose details in dev
  });
});

// Catch unhandled promise rejections (async route errors)
process.on('unhandledRejection', (reason) => {
  console.error('Unhandled rejection:', reason);
  process.exit(1); // Let process manager (PM2, K8s) restart cleanly
});
```

